  "solution": {
    "text": "From the rating of the bulb, the resistance of the bulb can be calculated.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>P</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image1-77838b5f-e7f5-4d4f-89c1-cb5df4bdc2f0.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"height: 144px; width: 280px;\" /><br /><br />For the bulb to be operated at its rated value the rms current through it should be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math><br /><br />Also,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>200</mn><msqrt><msup><mn>100</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mn>5</mn><mn>0</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mi>L</mi><mtext> </mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>",
